        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "1cbd393e-7223-5ee2-b2da-22b0d48db09e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Clinchfield Railroad, Union Pacific Railroad, Yancey Railroad, Chesapeake and Ohio Railway\n- Places: Dante, Virginia; Elkhorn City; Sandy Ridge Mountains; Kona, North Carolina; Micaville; Burnsville\n- Products: Challenger locomotives\n- Topics: railroad routes, freight service, coal transport connections\n\nFacts:\n- Challenger locomotives were most common on the Union Pacific Railroad and the Clinchfield Railroad.\n- In 1915, the Clinchfield Railroad completed a 35-mile segment from Dante, Virginia, to Elkhorn City.\n- The Clinchfield Railroad segment opened coal lands north of the Sandy Ridge Mountains and formed a connection with the Chesapeake and Ohio Railway at Elkhorn City.\n- The Yancey Railroad was an American Class III shortline railroad with reporting mark YAN.\n- The Yancey Railroad operated freight service for 10.6 miles from a connection with the Clinchfield Railroad at Kona, North Carolina, through Micaville, to Burnsville.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
